<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong to build hospital in Malaysia.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong to build hospital in Malaysia.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ssangyong Engineering &amp; Construction Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's Ssangyong Group, said it had won a $120 million order with its Japanese partner Obayashi Corp to build a hospital in Kuala Lumpur.</p>
<p>A Ssangyong spokesman said Ssangyong's stake was worth $70 million and Obayashi would invest $50 million.</p>
<p>Construction of the 964-room hospital will begin in October with completion scheduled for August 1998.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5642</p>
</text>
